	skos:definition "A negative modulation mechanism in which an effector small interfering RNA (siRNA) molecule finds and destroys messenger RNA (mRNA) with a complementary sequence, preventing a specific gene from being translated into a protein. Note that while this is called \"inhibition', it is not inhibition in the classic biochemical sense that requires a direct interaction between effector and target." .
biolink:CausalMechanismQualifierEnum\#s_nitrosylation a owl:Class ;
	rdfs:label "s_nitrosylation" ;
	rdfs:subClassOf biolink:CausalMechanismQualifierEnum\#molecular_modification , biolink:CausalMechanismQualifierEnum .
