	skos:definition "An association between a gene (or gene product) and a disease for which the gene is statistically correlated with the disease rather than asserted as causal. Such associations typically derive from GWAS, co-occurrence analyses, or other statistical methods, and are annotated with scores such as a z-score or a diseases confidence score." ;
	skos:inScheme biolink: .
